<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jayajirao Scindia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1835–1886</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jayajirao Scindia was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharaja">Maharaja</a> of Gwalior from 1843 to 1886. During the rebellion of 1857 he remained loyal to the British, though much of his army joined the rebels, and in 1858 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lakshmibai">Rani of Jhansi</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tatya-tope">Tatya Tope</a> briefly seized Gwalior fort before British forces retook it. He was rewarded with territory and honours and built the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jai-vilas-palace">Jai Vilas Palace</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jayajirao-scindia.jpg" alt="Jayajirao Scindia" width="250" height="340" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jayaji_Rao_Scindia.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
